g wording kept. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E002, RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Split across the component boundary the HLR itself spans: Model Registry backend records/exposes the run-of-origin linkage (E002); the Dashboard registry view surfaces the \"open comparison\" entry point (E003). The Dashboard portion is a distinct, deferrable P1 feature on a different UI surface (model-version view vs. runs list) gated on the registry linkage — bundling it into the P0 comparison epic would gate P0 work on P1 registry linkage (priority inversion). |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | docs-authoring epic; priority P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1). |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Component Classification\n\n- **Dashboard** — active (comparison view, registry entry point). Owning team\n  per architecture context: RHOAI Dashboard.\n- **Model Registry** — active (run-of-origin linkage on model versions).\n  Owning team per architecture context: Model Registry.\n- **Data Science Pipelines** — passive. The strategy implies no DSP code\n  change: run parameters/metrics are already recorded and surfaced on per-run\n  pages, and the Dashboard reads run data through existing interfaces.\n  Validation is folded into the nearest active epic (E001) as an acceptance\n  criterion: the comparison must correctly render parameters and metrics for\n  pipeline runs as well as training runs. No separate validation epic is\n  generated because no different-team validation responsibility is stated; see\n  Health Warnings for the verification caveat.\n\n## Component Name Mapping\n\nAll epic `component` values are copied verbatim from\n`.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Dashboard`, `Model Registry`, and\n`Documentation` (for the docs-authoring epic). No non-obvious mappings were\nneeded; the strategy's affected-component names already match canonical names.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n  and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Teams were derived from the\n  architecture-context owning teams; epic acceptance criteria were derived from\n  the HLRs. The docs epic's owning team is not stated anywhere in the strategy\n  or context — assigned to \"RHOAI Docs\"; verify with the strategy author.\n- **Passive-component assumption to verify:** the decomposition assumes\n  pipeline-run parameters and metrics are consistently recorded and retrievable\n  for comparison (the strategy asserts they live on per-run pages). If review\n  finds gaps in pipeline-run metadata capture, a Data Science Pipelines epic\n  owned by RHOAI Pipelines would need to be added.\n- **HLR consolidation:** HLR-1 and HLR-3 are consolidated into a single epic\n  (see the traceability matrix row for the rationale). This is deliberate, not\n  an omission — the strategy's own note that overlapping wording was kept from\n  two customer councils corroborates that the two HLRs describe one capability.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\nin-platform.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37351,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b411dbfd314d8f25","agent_id":"aa954b0a9e3296286","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"fb1e896c-bb05-4a5a-b172-3ac901b585ff","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:20:50.418Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
