{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a35f250d-ac14-459e-ad73-f6218dec37f2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0af7a0979d2ff51","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-xgjy54om/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the run comparison capability in the Dashboard: users can\nselect two or more training or pipeline runs and view their parameters and\nmetrics side by side, including a diff presentation that highlights which\nparameters and metrics changed between two selected runs. Today parameters and\nmetrics live only on per-run pages, forcing data scientists to compare runs in\nexported spreadsheets; this epic brings that comparison in-platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs (training runs and Data Science Pipelines\n  runs) from the runs list in the Dashboard.\n- A side-by-side comparison view of the selected runs' parameters and metrics.\n- A diff presentation mode over the same comparison data that highlights which\n  parameters and metrics differ between two selected runs.\n- Correct rendering of runs with differing parameter/metric sets (values\n  present on one run and absent on another).\n- Comparison stays within a single project and cluster, consistent with the\n  strategy's out-of-scope statement (no cross-project or cross-cluster\n  comparison).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can select two or more runs from the runs list and open a comparison\n  showing each run's parameters and metrics side by side.\n- Given two selected runs, the comparison highlights which parameters and\n  metrics changed between them.\n- The comparison correctly renders parameters and metrics for Data Science\n  Pipelines runs as well as training runs (validation of the passive Data\n  Science Pipelines component — its run data is consumed as-is through\n  existing interfaces, with no pipelines-side changes).\n- The comparison handles runs whose parameter/metric sets differ without\n  errors or silent omission.\n- Comparison is offered only for runs within the same project and cluster.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): select two or more runs and view parameters and metrics side by\n  side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1, consolidated with HLR-1): run \"diff\" view highlighting which\n  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs — a presentation\n  mode of the same comparison surface, covered by this epic at the higher\n  priority rather than split into a separate epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39415,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b411dbfd314d8f25","agent_id":"aa954b0a9e3296286","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"673a1447-28f7-4088-9ae3-4f0f8b5ee9ee","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:21:01.416Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
