{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a35f250d-ac14-459e-ad73-f6218dec37f2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf0c7df36d8f3f6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-xgjy54om/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Record the producing run on registered model versions\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers run-of-origin lineage in the Model Registry: a registered\nmodel version records the identity of the run (training or pipeline run) that\nproduced it, and that linkage is exposed through the Model Registry's\ninterfaces so that a comparison can be opened from a registered model version.\nThis is the registry-side half of connecting model promotion decisions to the\nruns behind them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Ability to record, at or after registration, which run produced a given\n  registered model version, using the Model Registry's existing metadata\n  extension points for model versions (the exact mechanism — e.g. custom\n  properties versus a dedicated field — is an implementation decision for the\n  Model Registry team).\n- The run-of-origin linkage is retrievable per model version through the Model\n  Registry REST API so that UIs can resolve the producing run.\n- Registration flows and existing model versions are not broken: model\n  versions without a recorded producing run remain valid.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A registered model version can carry the identity of the run that produced\n  it, and that identity is retrievable through the Model Registry REST API for\n  a given model version.\n- Registering a model version without a producing-run reference still\n  succeeds (the linkage is optional metadata, not a required field).\n- The linkage round-trips through the API: a client can read back the same\n  producing-run identity it recorded for a model version.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them — registry-side recording and exposure of the linkage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39415,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b411dbfd314d8f25","agent_id":"aa954b0a9e3296286","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"4a37b53b-d50b-4d34-baf8-0af7753ecabf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:21:06.610Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
