{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-68eabd3b-9598-4992-966e-2cc12390504d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b40b68930cbacae1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-xgjy54om/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E003.md","content":"# Open run comparison from the Model Registry view in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Model Registry entry point to the run comparison\ncapability: from a registered model version viewed in the Dashboard's Model\nRegistry section, a user can open a comparison that includes the run that\nproduced that model version. Model promotion decisions then start from the\nregistry with side-by-side visibility into what changed between candidate\nruns, instead of requiring users to go find the runs in the runs list first.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic consumes two capabilities delivered elsewhere in the strategy and\ndoes not re-implement either: the run comparison view (parameters and metrics\nside by side, with diff highlighting) and the producing-run linkage recorded\non registered model versions and exposed through the Model Registry REST API.\nBoth must be available before this epic's work can complete.\n\n## Scope\n\n- In the Dashboard's Model Registry view, a model version that carries a\n  producing-run reference offers an action to open a comparison including that\n  run.\n- The action resolves the producing-run identity through the Model Registry\n  and navigates to the existing run comparison view with that run loaded,\n  letting the user add further runs to the comparison.\n- The entry point is hidden or disabled for model versions that carry no\n  producing-run reference.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- From a registered model version in the Dashboard's Model Registry view that\n  has a recorded producing run, a user can open a comparison that includes\n  that run, rendered by the existing comparison view.\n- The user can add one or more further runs to the comparison opened this way,\n  for both training runs and pipeline runs.\n- Model versions without a producing-run reference show no broken entry point\n  (the action is absent or visibly disabled with a clear reason).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — the\n  Dashboard-side entry point over the registry linkage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40587,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b411dbfd314d8f25","agent_id":"aa954b0a9e3296286","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"c971dd2e-966a-46b9-8c97-455a416630ae","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:21:14.626Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
