{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87431a76fdb50ae3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n10\t\n11\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major. No Staff Engineer Input\n12\tsection is present, so the strategy's own requirement tables are authoritative.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans three affected components (Dashboard,\n17\tModel Registry, Data Science Pipelines) owned by at least two teams, and it\n18\tcontains multiple distinct work streams (Dashboard UI implementation, Model\n19\tRegistry backend implementation, and documentation authoring). Not docs-only:\n20\tcode changes are required. Full decomposition follows.\n21\t\n22\t## Epic List\n23\t\n24\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n25\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Record the producing run on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry view in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow from the runs list and the registry | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n30\t\n31\t## Dependency DAG\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 Run comparison view] --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 Registry entry point]\n36\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 Run-of-origin linkage] --> E003\n37\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 Documentation]\n38\t    E002 --> E004\n39\t    E003 --> E004\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tE001 and E002 are parallel roots (different components, different repos, no\n43\tshared artifacts — Rule 14).\n44\t\n45\t## DAG Justification\n46\t\n47\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n48\t|------|------|-----------|\n49\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The registry entry point navigates to and builds against the run comparison view; it must not re-implement the comparison surface. |\n50\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry entry point's code resolves the run-of-origin linkage that the Model Registry exposes; without the linkage data/API there is nothing to open a comparison from. |\n51\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the implemented comparison workflow. |\n52\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the registry-side linkage flow. |\n53\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers opening a comparison from the registry. |\n54\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components and repos with no shared artifacts; the comparison-from-runs-list value must not be gated on registry work. |\n55\t\n56\tNo onboarding-chain edges apply: Dashboard, Model Registry, and Data Science\n57\tPipelines all have architecture-context files and are already Konflux-onboarded,\n58\tso no `repo-onboarding`, `license-validation`, or `konflux-onboarding` epics are\n59\tgenerated (Rules 5–10, 20, 25 not triggered).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n62\t\n63\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n64\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n65\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Core comparison capability from the runs list. |\n66\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 (consolidated with HLR-1) — the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run parameters/metrics; a split would build the same surface twice plus an artificial serialization edge, so the epic covers both at the higher priority (P0) | Redundant/overlapping HLR, consolidated per the consolidation rule. The strategy itself notes the requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. |\n67\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E002, RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Split across the component boundary the HLR itself spans: Model Registry backend records/exposes the run-of-origin linkage (E002); the Dashboard registry view surfaces the \"open comparison\" entry point (E003). The Dashboard portion is a distinct, deferrable P1 feature on a different UI surface (model-version view vs. runs list) gated on the registry linkage — bundling it into the P0 comparison epic would gate P0 work on P1 registry linkage (priority inversion). |\n68\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | docs-authoring epic; priority P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1). |\n69\t\n70\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n71\t\n72\t## Component Classification\n73\t\n74\t- **Dashboard** — active (comparison view, registry entry point). Owning team\n75\t  per architecture context: RHOAI Dashboard.\n76\t- **Model Registry** — active (run-of-origin linkage on model versions).\n77\t  Owning team per architecture context: Model Registry.\n78\t- **Data Science Pipelines** — passive. The strategy implies no DSP code\n79\t  change: run parameters/metrics are already recorded and surfaced on per-run\n80\t  pages, and the Dashboard reads run data through existing interfaces.\n81\t  Validation is folded into the nearest active epic (E001) as an acceptance\n82\t  criterion: the comparison must correctly render parameters and metrics for\n83\t  pipeline runs as well as training runs. No separate validation epic is\n84\t  generated because no different-team validation responsibility is stated; see\n85\t  Health Warnings for the verification caveat.\n86\t\n87\t## Component Name Mapping\n88\t\n89\tAll epic `component` values are copied verbatim from\n90\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Dashboard`, `Model Registry`, and\n91\t`Documentation` (for the docs-authoring epic). No non-obvious mappings were\n92\tneeded; the strategy's affected-component names already match canonical names.\n93\t\n94\t## Health Warnings\n95\t\n96\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted\n97\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n98\t  and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Teams were derived from the\n99\t  architecture-context owning teams; epic acceptance criteria were derived from\n100\t  the HLRs. The docs epic's owning team is not stated anywhere in the strategy\n101\t  or context — assigned to \"RHOAI Docs\"; verify with the strategy author.\n102\t- **Passive-component assumption to verify:** the decomposition assumes\n103\t  pipeline-run parameters and metrics are consistently recorded and retrievable\n104\t  for comparison (the strategy asserts they live on per-run pages). If review\n105\t  finds gaps in pipeline-run metadata capture, a Data Science Pipelines epic\n106\t  owned by RHOAI Pipelines would need to be added.\n107\t- **HLR consolidation:** HLR-1 and HLR-3 are consolidated into a single epic\n108\t  (see the traceability matrix row for the rationale). This is deliberate, not\n109\t  an omission — the strategy's own note that overlapping wording was kept from\n110\t  two customer councils corroborates that the two HLRs describe one capability.\n111\t\n112\t## Tiered Delivery\n113\t\n114\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n115\tin-platform.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857d21ecca0f3048","agent_id":"a44c080f0f8d2aad2","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"fd6c6863-eeac-4ef9-88be-0f8fd643018a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:25:27.354Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87431a76fdb50ae3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"gener