{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a74e3aeea0f0b679","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Record the producing run on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Record the producing run on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers run-of-origin lineage in the Model Registry: a registered\n34\tmodel version records the identity of the run (training or pipeline run) that\n35\tproduced it, and that linkage is exposed through the Model Registry's\n36\tinterfaces so that a comparison can be opened from a registered model version.\n37\tThis is the registry-side half of connecting model promotion decisions to the\n38\truns behind them.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Ability to record, at or after registration, which run produced a given\n43\t  registered model version, using the Model Registry's existing metadata\n44\t  extension points for model versions (the exact mechanism — e.g. custom\n45\t  properties versus a dedicated field — is an implementation decision for the\n46\t  Model Registry team).\n47\t- The run-of-origin linkage is retrievable per model version through the Model\n48\t  Registry REST API so that UIs can resolve the producing run.\n49\t- Registration flows and existing model versions are not broken: model\n50\t  versions without a recorded producing run remain valid.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A registered model version can carry the identity of the run that produced\n55\t  it, and that identity is retrievable through the Model Registry REST API for\n56\t  a given model version.\n57\t- Registering a model version without a producing-run reference still\n58\t  succeeds (the linkage is optional metadata, not a required field).\n59\t- The linkage round-trips through the API: a client can read back the same\n60\t  producing-run identity it recorded for a model version.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n65\t  them — registry-side recording and exposure of the linkage.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857d21ecca0f3048","agent_id":"a44c080f0f8d2aad2","session_id":"e17dd9cb-088d-45af-9a10-58f6765a919b","uuid":"89e7b0cb-bd14-4d29-9015-fbb27d8fe082","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:25:28.574Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a74e3aeea0f0b679","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
